WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.080
- Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.150
We are here with Hannah
Waddingham and Reid Scott.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:03.983
Give it up.

00:00:03.983 --> 00:00:05.850
(audience cheering)
(Kelly clapping)

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.490
So that was a look at
Reid in the new fifth

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.740
and final season of The
Marvelous Mrs. Maisel.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.420
You can see it on Prime Video.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:13.770
So thank you so much for hosting our game.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:14.603
You were killer.
- Thank you.

00:00:14.603 --> 00:00:15.870
- You nailed it.
- I had a great time.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:16.703
That was fun.

00:00:16.703 --> 00:00:17.560
- And you gave personal stories.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:18.540
I like it, I like it.
- Yeah, oh yeah.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.440
I'm an open book.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:20.550
- I get it, me too.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:21.598
My mom doesn't love it.

00:00:21.598 --> 00:00:22.431
(all three chuckling)

00:00:22.431 --> 00:00:25.020
So did playing a host
on Marvelous Mrs. Maisel

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.360
did it help prepare for this job?

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.026
- For this?
- Yes, cause you killed it.

00:00:29.026 --> 00:00:31.350
I just thought there
was some method there.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.293
- That's why I took the job.

00:00:32.293 --> 00:00:33.126
- It's all been leading to this.

00:00:33.126 --> 00:00:33.959
- Yes, exactly.

00:00:33.959 --> 00:00:35.213
I took the job on Mrs. Maisel
cause I knew that I was going

00:00:35.213 --> 00:00:36.720
to play a host on...
- So you could prep.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.370
Exactly, thank you.
- On give me a line.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:39.630
- We like to set the bar.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:40.830
- It was a great experience.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:41.663
It really was.

00:00:41.663 --> 00:00:45.150
I got to do research in a way
that I hadn't done before.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.430
I always research whatever
character I'm doing a bit

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:48.660
to try to get inside the head...

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.010
- Yeah.
- Of that type of person.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.330
But this was so specific.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:52.530
And I grew up...

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.766
You know, my formative
years were the nineties,

00:00:54.766 --> 00:00:55.674
- Me too.

00:00:55.674 --> 00:00:57.780
- So the talk show scene between Conan

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:58.613
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:58.613 --> 00:00:59.800
- And I think some of the
very best of David Letterman.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.320
- Yeah, yeah.
- You know, Jay Leno

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:02.790
at his prime.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.320
Those were my nights as a kid.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:05.153
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:05.153 --> 00:01:05.986
- I revered them,

00:01:05.986 --> 00:01:08.370
and I thought it was just
magical what hosts do.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:10.170
And I never thought in a
million years that would ever

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.790
be anything I would pursue.

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:13.260
And then I got to play a bit of a host.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.900
My character morphed into a host on Veep.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:16.740
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.490
- Where I played this total (beep).

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:20.483
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:20.483 --> 00:01:21.779
- Which you can't bleep it
out if I spell that, right?

00:01:21.779 --> 00:01:22.680
You can't bleep it out if I spell it.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.456
- Which are fun characters to play, right?

00:01:24.456 --> 00:01:25.289
That seems like

00:01:25.289 --> 00:01:26.122
a more fun character.
- They're super fun.

00:01:26.122 --> 00:01:26.955
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah.
- Oh, it was the best.

00:01:26.955 --> 00:01:29.580
And he played a host on
CBS and was really great

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:33.180
cause it was very satirical
how we sort of approached it.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.980
And then when this came up on Maisel,

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.590
which is just an incredible
show, so beautifully written

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:38.700
and beautifully shot,
- [Kelly] For sure.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.800
- they said they wanted to
sort of explore this guy,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.510
kind of like a young Johnny Carson.

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:44.370
And I was like, oh wow,
that's really interesting

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.203
to me.
- Wow.

00:01:45.203 --> 00:01:46.920
- It was just so fun to play in that space

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:50.220
but then also play the
duality of what it's like

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:51.690
when this guy who...

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.820
I'm making a career out of playing jerks,

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:54.949
which I don't know what that says.

00:01:54.949 --> 00:01:55.782
(Kelly and Hannah laughing)

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.510
But what it's like when they yell cut.

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.040
What is he like when he goes home?

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.930
What is he like with his writing staff?

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.596
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- What is he like with Midge?

00:02:02.596 --> 00:02:04.320
Who she comes on, they sort of,

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:05.610
they start to work
together in a bit of a way.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.230
I don't want to give too much of it away,

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:11.760
but it was just great to sort
of feel those switches flip

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.230
in between the different personalities

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.400
that he sort of has to present:

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.990
one to the camera, one to the audience,

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.820
one to America, one to his staff.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.226
- You just made acting sound really cool.

00:02:20.226 --> 00:02:21.059
- Oh wow.
(Hannah and Reid laughing)

00:02:21.059 --> 00:02:22.721
- Cause I love research.
- Yeah.

00:02:22.721 --> 00:02:24.880
- And I love all the
development that goes into it.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:25.950
- Yeah.
- [Kelly] That's exciting.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.050
- But even if a character
is like, like you're saying,

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.660
not particularly nice or
they have this about them,

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:33.630
you have to fall in love
with all aspects of them...

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:34.890
- [Kelly] Mm hmm.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.150
- To give them somebody else.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.100
- [Reid] Exactly.
- I think.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:38.933
- It's so exciting.

00:02:38.933 --> 00:02:40.260
Yeah, you made it really, really exciting.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.093
So wait...
- [Reid] Thank you.

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:42.300
We don't wanna be rude, but we had some

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.410
of Hannah's ice cream earlier.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:44.910
So we wanted to offer you
some just sitting here.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:45.743
- Oh my god.

00:02:45.743 --> 00:02:46.814
Don't offer him the one I was going at.

00:02:46.814 --> 00:02:48.144
(Reid and Kelly laughing)

00:02:48.144 --> 00:02:49.380
- Oh, this is for me too?
- Just in case you wanted

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.213
to try it.

00:02:50.213 --> 00:02:51.046
- Comes with an ice cream glove.

00:02:51.046 --> 00:02:51.879
- Look, I'm Southern.

00:02:51.879 --> 00:02:52.890
I know, right, like what?

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.183
Were we in the snow?
- It's very chic.

00:02:54.183 --> 00:02:55.016
(Hannah and Kelly laughing)

00:02:55.016 --> 00:02:56.130
- This is, oh my God.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:57.060
- Yes.
- Wow.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:57.893
- You're having...

00:02:57.893 --> 00:02:59.880
[All Three] Biscuits with the boss.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.546
- [Kelly] Just try it out. Just try it on.

00:03:01.546 --> 00:03:02.379
You can leave it here if you'd want.

00:03:02.379 --> 00:03:03.212
You don't have to...

00:03:03.212 --> 00:03:04.045
- Oh, damn, that's good.

00:03:04.045 --> 00:03:04.878
- It is good.
- Yeah, okay.

00:03:04.878 --> 00:03:06.480
It's kind of like shortbread ice cream.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.410
- It's like comfort food.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.390
- Oh, it's the shortbread from the show.

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:10.349
- [All three] Yeah.

00:03:10.349 --> 00:03:11.182
- Oh my God, that's really good.

00:03:11.182 --> 00:03:12.015
- [Kelly] Yeah, that's
what it tastes like.

00:03:12.015 --> 00:03:12.848
I never had it.

00:03:12.848 --> 00:03:13.681
Okay.
- Isn't it gorgeous?

00:03:13.681 --> 00:03:14.514
- So I heard that you now have...

00:03:14.514 --> 00:03:15.347
I want you to have food in your mouth

00:03:15.347 --> 00:03:17.013
when I ask this next
question. (all three laughing)

00:03:17.013 --> 00:03:18.600
I heard that you now have a bad habit

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:19.800
when you're out with your kids.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:20.633
What is it?

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.890
- Oh, oh, with my mouth.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.270
- What's wrong with your mouth?

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.301
- That's not a sentence you hear everyday.

00:03:26.301 --> 00:03:27.646
- Yeah, okay.
(everyone laughing)

00:03:27.646 --> 00:03:28.757
- I swear a lot.

00:03:28.757 --> 00:03:29.590
- Oh, me too.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:30.500
- I have a filthy mouth.
- [Hannah] Oh God.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:31.881
- Me too.
- I have a very filthy mouth.

00:03:31.881 --> 00:03:33.384
- Look, I was a waitress.
- Good man.

00:03:33.384 --> 00:03:34.217
- Thank you, right?

00:03:34.217 --> 00:03:35.335
- Yeah, I just, yeah...

00:03:35.335 --> 00:03:36.194
- I was a waitress.

00:03:36.194 --> 00:03:38.190
- Look, people, they make you mad

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:39.690
and darn it doesn't cover it.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.370
Yeah, like, yeah.
(Hannah laughing)

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:42.203
- Not in this town.

00:03:42.203 --> 00:03:43.470
- Yeah, what is your...

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.480
Do you have a rule with your kids though?

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.147
- Well, it's morphed over the years.

00:03:47.147 --> 00:03:47.980
- Okay.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:49.740
- So my kids are almost
eight and just turned five.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:50.573
- [Hannah] Ah.

00:03:50.573 --> 00:03:52.740
- Like I tried the swear jar for a while.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:53.573
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:03:53.573 --> 00:03:54.406
My kids would be rich.
- That's gonna get full.

00:03:54.406 --> 00:03:56.520
Yeah, yeah.
- It filled up so fast

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.920
that I was just using it to
like tip any delivery person

00:03:58.920 --> 00:03:59.940
that came to the house.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.260
This is not what the swear jar is for.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.093
- No.

00:04:02.093 --> 00:04:03.840
- Or it was like, you
know, tooth fairy money.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:04.673
- Love it.
- Yeah.

00:04:04.673 --> 00:04:06.750
- And so I realized, all
right, that's not gonna work.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.460
It's not the deterrent that I need.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:12.090
What really sort of brought
it home is I was driving

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.970
with my son, Conrad, and
someone ran out in front

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:17.850
of the car, and I
screamed like, oh my god,

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:19.290
you bleeping bleep.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:20.123
- [Hannah] Yeah.

00:04:20.123 --> 00:04:22.020
- And then everything was fine,

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:24.030
and I kept on driving, and
I hear this little voice

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.120
from the back go, Dada,
what's a bleeping bleep?

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:27.953
- Oh.

00:04:27.953 --> 00:04:29.070
- And I'm like, oh...

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:29.903
- Don't tell Mommy.

00:04:29.903 --> 00:04:31.569
- Yeah, don't tell Mom. It
was just something, you know.

00:04:31.569 --> 00:04:32.402
Daddy got angry.

00:04:32.402 --> 00:04:33.780
And he's like, oh, okay.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.010
And then maybe two days later

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:36.840
the exact same thing happened again.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.010
Like someone on a bike went right

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:38.843
in front of the car.

00:04:38.843 --> 00:04:39.676
Like, oh my God.

00:04:39.676 --> 00:04:40.830
The exact same expletives.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:42.090
You bleeping bleep!

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:45.180
And then Conrad again is like, Dada,

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.620
there's those words again.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:47.610
I'm like, yeah, son, yeah.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:48.648
Really, really sorry about that.

00:04:48.648 --> 00:04:49.560
(Hannah laughing)

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.410
Then maybe a week later,
I'm outside at the grill.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:53.250
I'm having a good time.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.660
I'm grilling up some food.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:58.140
And our younger son was an infant.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.780
And my wife comes out, and she's tired,

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:01.770
and she's bouncing the baby.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:03.840
She's like, I just want you
to know what your son said.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:05.940
He said, I want to kiss my baby brother.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:07.459
I want to kiss that bleeping bleep.

00:05:07.459 --> 00:05:10.000
(audience laughing)
(Hannah clapping and laughing)

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.450
- Oh, that's when you go,
where did he hear that?

00:05:13.368 --> 00:05:15.453
- That's certainly not from me.

00:05:15.453 --> 00:05:16.410
- That's crazy.
- Things they hear

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:17.760
at school these days.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:19.440
- So I've had to rein
it back in a little bit.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:20.640
And now my kids think it's a joke.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.710
They're like, you're doing it again, Dad.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.120
- Look, it colors a sentence.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:28.620
- Look, I tell my kids that they can curse

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.510
when they pay their bills.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.895
You have to earn being this trashy.

00:05:32.895 --> 00:05:34.367
You have to earn it.
(everyone laughing)

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:36.790
I was like, you can't do it.
- It's good enough for Dolly.

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:38.070
- Like, do whatever you want.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.350
- Be as class as you
want when you're older.

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:41.183
- [Reid] Yeah.
- [Hannah] That's brilliant.

00:05:41.183 --> 00:05:42.120
- But like right now you can't do it.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:42.953
- Yeah.

00:05:42.953 --> 00:05:44.430
- Cause I'm like, I'm
not gonna just alter...

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:46.350
I'm not like, I don't curse
that much in front of them,

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:48.570
but like every now and then I'll slip up,

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:49.440
and then they'll be like, oh.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:50.550
And I'm like, nah, nah, nah, nah, nah.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:51.383
Don't even talk about it.

00:05:51.383 --> 00:05:53.400
- My daughter has no
hope coming from theater.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.347
She's got a right potty
mouth for a mother.

00:05:55.347 --> 00:05:56.684
- I think that's the problem.
- Terrible.

00:05:56.684 --> 00:05:57.517
- Yeah.

00:05:57.517 --> 00:05:58.440
- But they need to see all sides of you.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.970
- [Reid] Exactly.
- Yeah.

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:01.260
I'm just trying to show you all sides

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.093
of humanity.
- In moderation.

00:06:02.093 --> 00:06:03.360
(Hannah laughing)
(Kelly laughing and clapping)

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.340
All right, we need another
commercial break everybody,

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.690
but you can see the final season

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:09.393
of The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel
right now on Prime Video.

